     2	  "The REPL's standard frontend catalog (docs/design/yang.antlr.md section
     3	   8.5.6, slice F2): the three legacy hand-written frontends installed into
     4	   a `yang.frontend` catalog. This is the only place the REPL composition
     5	   names a language's namespace; `yin.repl` core steps whatever binding the
     6	   catalog selects.
     7	
     8	   A binding is `{:parse (fn [input]) :lower (fn [parsed])}`, with
     9	   `:input :forms` when the frontend consumes the forms the shell reader
    10	   already read, else the source text."
